1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,600
Amara Okafor: Good morning everyone, let us start with
the release four point two readiness.

2
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:20,674
Léa Fontaine: The build is green on every runner, but
the German locale files still have forty

3
00:00:20,674 --> 00:00:24,900
seven untranslated strings and nobody has
proof-read them yet.

4
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,100
Sorry, could you repeat the last figure?

5
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:33,000
Léa Fontaine: Forty seven strings, all of them in the
billing screens.

6
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,400
Amara Okafor: Understood.

7
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:16,234
Then we ship four point two on the twelfth
of June with the German locale disabled,

8
00:06:16,234 --> 00:06:19,800
and we open a follow-up ticket for the
translations.

9
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,355
Jonas Weber: On the incident of last Tuesday: the pager
fired at two in the morning, the responder

10
00:10:46,355 --> 00:10:51,500
had already worked a full week, and the
hand-over notes were missing.

11
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:38,400
Amara Okafor: Agreed, we move the rotation to a two-week
cycle starting in July.

12
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Léa Fontaine: For the transcription cluster we need two
more GPU nodes to keep the queue under ten

13
00:19:47,713 --> 00:19:49,200
minutes at peak.

14
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,800
Amara Okafor: Approved. Please draft the procurement
request before the board meeting.
